  "slug": "automated-enables-08a1",
  "summary": "Cryo-ET, fluorescence-guided FIB milling and ptychographic cryo-EM now combine large-area, targeted and near-atomic readouts in cells and parasite samples.",
  "synthesis": "The shared thread is automation of electron microscopy workflows that make nanoscale ultrastructure both targetable and quantifiable. A stitched 3D cryo-electron tomography montage reveals heterogeneous yet connected Arp2/3 branched actin networks across lamellipodia of migrating cells. Fluorescence-guided 3D FIB milling is introduced for locating rare structures in high-pressure-frozen samples, validated by recovery of centrosomes. Ptychographic single-particle cryo-EM adds automated probe estimation and dose-fractionation, reaching 3.3 Å resolution. Deep-learning-assisted FIB-SEM reconstructs Plasmodium falciparum oocyst ultrastructure and segments sporozoites synchronously. What is new is the combination of fluorescence-guided targeting, automated parameter estimation and deep-learning segmentation for volumetric imaging of rare structures. All four items are preprints, so the evidence remains unreviewed.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-27"
}
